"ai_prompt_hint" = "Copy the prompt below to any AI assistant (Doubao, ChatGPT…), send your timetable screenshot, then paste the AI output back into the text field above to import.";
"ai_prompt_text" = "Task: Convert the timetable screenshot (or file content) I send next into the sleepy-v1 plain-text format. Output nothing besides the conversion result itself - no explanations, no greetings, no markdown code fences. The first line of your output must be #sleepy-v1.\\n\\n========== 1. Format rules ==========\\n\\nThe first line is always: #sleepy-v1\\n\\nEvery other line is one record, with columns separated by a vertical bar |. Three kinds of lines:\\n\\n1. T line (table info, optional, at most one):\\nTtableName|termStartDate|totalWeeks|nodesPerDay\\n· The start date format is YYYY-MM-DD and must be the Monday of week 1\\n· Fill in only what the timetable explicitly states; leave unspecified fields empty. You may stop after the last known column, e.g. T|2026-03-02\\n· If the timetable does not mention these at all, omit the T line entirely. Never guess.\\n\\n2. N line (per-period times, optional, one line per period):\\nNnumber|startTime|endTime\\n· e.g. N3|10:00|10:45\\n· Only output N lines if the timetable explicitly provides a period-time table. Use 24-hour HH:mm; write 8:00 as 08:00\\n· No period-time table in the timetable -> output no N lines at all\\n\\n3. C line (courses, the main body, one line per occurrence):\\nCname|day|nodes|weeks|teacher|room|color|note|time|group\\nAlways exactly 10 columns / 9 bars. Empty columns stay empty, but the bars must not be dropped. Column rules:\\n  Col 1 name: copy the timetable verbatim, character for character, any language\\n  Col 2 day: Monday..Sunday = 1 2 3 4 5 6 7\\n  Col 3 nodes: periods 3-4 = 3-4; single period 6 = 6\\n  Col 4 weeks: see \"2. Week rules\"\\n  Col 5 teacher: copy from the timetable; empty if absent\\n  Col 6 room: same\\n  Col 7 color: always empty\\n  Col 8 note: only if the timetable states a note; otherwise empty\\n  Col 9 time: only when the timetable explicitly marks a clock time for this course (e.g. an evening/non-standard-time class), as HH:mm-HH:mm; this is the private course start/end time and must not be added as an N period-time row; otherwise empty\\n  Col 10 group: always empty\\n\\n========== 2. Week rules ==========\\n\\nExtract the set of weeks each course meets, then decide in order:\\n1. A continuous range with no odd/even restriction -> S-E, e.g. 1-16\\n2. All odd weeks within the range (\"odd weeks\") -> S-E单, e.g. 1-15单\\n3. All even weeks (\"even weeks\") -> S-E双, e.g. 2-16双\\n4. Scattered weeks (e.g. \"weeks 1-8, 10, 12-16\") -> split into maximal runs, one C line each, copying all other columns:\\n   · A full-week run -> S-E (e.g. 1-8, 12-16)\\n   · A lone single week -> S定 (e.g. 10定)\\n   · A purely odd run -> S-E单; a purely even run -> S-E双\\n   · A run that is neither continuous nor purely odd/even -> S-E定 (e.g. weeks 6,7 -> 6-7定)\\n5. The timetable says nothing about weeks -> 1-16\\n\\n========== 3. Extraction rules ==========\\n\\n· A course meeting multiple times per week (different days or periods) -> multiple C lines, one per meeting; never merge into one line\\n· Read period numbers from \"period X\" in the timetable; if it has only times and no periods, number the non-overlapping time slots 1, 2, 3... top to bottom and emit matching N lines\\n· Copy names, teachers and rooms verbatim; if a text contains |  \" < { ( escape each with a leading ; a newline inside text is the two characters \\n and a tab is \\t\\n· Anything the timetable does not state stays empty. Never invent teachers, rooms, times or weeks.\\n\\n========== 4. Output self-check (verify silently, do not print) ==========\\n\\n· First line is #sleepy-v1 and nothing else precedes or follows the records\\n· Every C line has exactly 9 bars / 10 columns\\n· Day is a digit 1-7; hours are two digits (08:00, not 8:00)\\n· The weeks column only ever shows S-E, S-E单, S-E双, S-E定 or S定\\n· Names match the timetable verbatim; nothing was invented\\n\\n========== 5. Example output ==========\\n\\n#sleepy-v1\\nT|2026-03-02\\nN1|08:00|08:45\\nN2|08:55|09:40\\nN3|10:00|10:45\\nN4|10:55|11:40\\nN5|14:00|14:45\\nN6|14:55|15:40\\nN7|16:00|16:45\\nN8|16:55|17:40\\nN9|19:00|19:45\\nN10|19:55|20:40\\nC高等数学A|1|1-2|1-16|张三|A101||||\\nC高等数学A|3|3-4|1-16|张三|A101||||\\nC大学英语|2|3-4|1-15单|李四|C301||||\\nC数据结构|4|3-4|2-16双|王五|C302||||\\nC体育|4|5-6|3-4定||||||\\nCJava实战|3|9-10|1-16||机房|||19:00-21:30|\\nC影视鉴赏|7|6|10-16双||||||\\nC形势与政策|5|8-9|1-8||||||\\nC形势与政策|5|8-9|12-16||||||";
